  "jcr:description": "The subtalar joint (talocalcaneal joint) is a common source of arthritis, often seen in hindfoot deformity, inflammatory conditions, or following calcaneus fractures. An arthrodesis in this location fuses the joint to eliminate movement, thus helping to correct deformity and improve symptoms.",
